  "shorts"
 ],
 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "Your valley floods every spring, so you decide to build a dam and hold the water back.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "You pile up dirt across the valley, and the lake fills up behind it. Problem solved!",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But water slowly soaks into the dirt and leaks out the other side.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Worse, it carries a little soil with it, and the leak grows into a tunnel.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you build a core of packed clay in the middle. Water can barely pass through it.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "On the dry side, a gravel filter lets the last drops out but keeps the soil in.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then a giant storm hits. The lake rises, and rises, until it spills over the top.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Water running over a dirt dam is the worst thing that can happen.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "It eats the slope away, and in minutes the whole dam can wash out.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "That's what happened above Derna, in Libya, in 2023. Experts think the spillways were too small for the storm.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you add a big concrete spillway, a safe path for extra water to leave.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Now the lake can never climb to the top of the dirt.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Big rocks on the water side stop the waves from chewing the slope.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "And someone has to inspect it every year, because old dams fail quietly.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Congratulations! You just built a dam that survives the storm. What should we build next?",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
 ],
